course: dictionary
lesson: 5217
title: Jealous and feelings words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Jealous is a feeling word. It means you are unhappy or upset because someone has something you want, such as a toy, success or attention. «He feels jealous and a bit forgotten.» The word forgotten is a clue: he feels left out, so jealous is about wanting what someone else has.
explain: Context helps you spot the meaning. «Chloe, who had got a sticker that week, felt hot and jealous and tore the certificate in half.» Hot and tearing up a certificate show a strong, angry feeling. Chloe was not happy for her friend. She was upset that someone else had something she wanted.
explain: Jealous is a normal feeling. Everyone has it sometimes. The important thing is what you do with it. You can name the feeling, say it to a trusted adult, and try not to be unkind. Stories often show a jealous character causing trouble, so noticing the feeling early helps.
fact: Jealous is an adjective. You can also say more jealous and most jealous.
fact: «Jealous» means unhappy or upset because someone has something you want.
fact: Jealous can also mean worried that someone you love likes another person more than you.
fact: Useful phrases: «jealous of», «feel jealous», and «green with jealousy».
fact: Jealousy is a normal feeling. Everyone has feelings such as happy, sad, angry and jealous, and what matters is what we do with them.
exercise: «He feels jealous and a bit forgotten.» What does jealous mean here? | Tired after a long day | *Upset because someone else has something he wants | Very excited about a party | Hungry for lunch
exercise: «Chloe felt hot and jealous and tore the certificate in half.» What feeling made Chloe tear the certificate? | *Jealousy, which made her unkind | Joy | Boredom | Tiredness
exercise: Which words make a phrase with jealous from the lessons? | jealous sea | *jealous of | jealous dinner | jealous running
test: Is feeling jealous wrong? | It is wrong, so never feel it at all | It means you are a bad friend | *It is a normal feeling, and what we do with it matters | It only happens to grown-ups
test: What helps when you feel jealous? | Pretend it is not there and say nothing ever | Hide the feeling and be unkind | *Name the feeling and talk about it with a trusted adult | Hit someone or tear up their things
exam: Which word from «love is patient and kind, not jealous, boastful, proud or rude» is a good thing to be? | jealous | rude | boastful | *patient
